## Remember
- This library is a learning tool AND production code - balance exploration with reliability
- Users range from beginners to your production team - design for the beginner, document for the expert
- Every line of code should answer: "Does this make the developer's life easier?"
- ABCs for contracts, explicit methods for access, clear visibility for every attribute
- Decorators ALWAYS work with both sync and async — no exceptions
- Observer integration everywhere — if it happens, we should be able to query it later
- Internal modules use `_internal.log`, external users use `observe` — prevents circular imports
- Formatting presets flow through both paths — `observe` and `_internal.log` respect config
- SQLite first, scale later — local-first design with upgrade path to Redis/Postgres
- Track everything in `.migration/FEATURE_GUIDE.md` — our secondary memory for v3 migration
- Simple things simple, complex things possible — YAGNI with an escape hatch
- Tests are mandatory — 95%+ coverage, organized by functionality, edge cases covered
- Test docstrings use emoji prefixes — matches Scriptman's visual language everywhere
